Z||000000||Gokart||03-07-2000||06:25 AM||||Even though the solenoid in my parts car had been sitting for a good 3 years or so I think my EGR problem is elsewhere. Could it be a vaccum leak? Guy at the Fiero Store says no it would just idle high, but a good mechanic told me yes? When I had the tube off after painting my plenum I used a wire wheel at both ends on the base to get the crap off it. Could I have taken off too much metal or an uneven amount off one side so the tube has a leak thus causing the code? I did the same with the plenum! I did tighten the plenum in the order shown in the Haynes manual, but I did not torque it, just tightened it down. So, could a vaccum leak at either base of the tube or plenum cause code 32? If not then I'm going to have to find ANOTHER solenoid! TIA for replys.||||reg||11
Z||000001||mwbackus||03-07-2000||02:28 PM||||Gokart,<BR>     There is a vacuum operated microswitch(2) on the EGR solenoid itself that triggers the code 32.  This switch basicly just monitors the presence (or lack of) vacuum TO the EGR valve.  If one looks closely at the routing and design of this system, it is apparent that a cracked EGR tube in itself cannot even set a code 32.  Look closer at the condition of the EGR solenoid, check for any cracked vacuum lines running into the valve, shorts or corrosion in the electrical connector/harness(1).  The filter(5) can be removed quite easily for cleaning, and the whole solenoid(4) can be dissassembled (carefully), and cleaned up a bit.  This design is prone to internal corrosion of the electrical terminals.  It is little more than an electromagnet with a core of thin delicate copper windings.  The points where these windings terminate and connect to the power source should be inspected for breaks.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/EGRSolenoid.jpg"> <P>Note : Image compliments of forum member - Rod, who was kind enough to scan this from the service manual.<p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 03-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||03-07-2000||08:24 PM||||Thanks nwbackus! So a vaccum leak at either end of the tube or plenum to intake manifold wiil NOT set code 32? I will inspect BOTH solenoids and take them apart for cleaning and check hoses/connectors.||||reg||14
